# par Noir — North star & Guiding Principles

This is why the repo exists. Local bugfixes that weaken this goal are wrong even if they compile.

## THE problem & Mission

Digital (and now AI) civilization has **no human root** — so every layer of power recentralizes away from persons. Platforms and AIs become principals; humans become the resource. Automation + AI collapsing barriers will amplify that unless persons are Layer 1 of the stack the world actually runs on — with privacy and speech as protocol defaults, not platform permissions.

## Core Architectural Axioms

- **Crypto without blockchain:** The cryptographic asset is decentralized identity, not a blockchain token. Identity is verified mathematically (pn file + pn name + passcode); no central server or chain. All three factors are required to unlock identity and everything on top.
- **User-owned, centralized to the user:** Users own their identity and custody their data directly (proof-of-work derivation; no central issuer). Real-world identity connects via ZKPs rather than data handover.
- **Platforms as aggregators:** Browsers and apps aggregate public files from users' Drives into feeds. Service providers leverage user infrastructure instead of hoarding user data.
- **par Noir 5-Layer Model:**
  - **Layer 1 (Identity):** PQC/PoW 3-factor identity derivation (`@par-noir/identity-crypto`).
  - **Layer 2 (Dashboard & Custody):** Personal identity management, secure cloud, and device custody.
  - **Layer 3 (API):** Owner routes and bridge connecting custody to tools.
  - **Layer 4 (Browser / Pen / Messaging):** Aggregation, authoring IR, and private E2E communications.
  - **Layer 5 (Third-Party Ecosystem):** Services building on user infrastructure without recentralization.

## No Plain-Text Sensitive Data

**Secrets or sensitive data points must never appear in plain text anywhere.** This applies to everything the identity protocol and ZKPs protect: **pn name, passcode, Google Drive account identifiers or tokens, age, email**, and any similar PII or credentials.
- **Where:** Not in code, server logs, console logs, error messages, debug output, or client wire payloads.
- **Enforcement:** Encrypt at rest and in transit, or expose only via ZKP/proof; never raw.

## Agent Obligations

Before implementing, verify:
1. Does this strengthen **human-as-root**, or create a landlord shortcut (app DB SoT, trust-the-client, agent-owned silo, soft-null on a credential path)?
2. Is there already a canonical module in `packages/` / API — or are we about to fork?
3. Avoid AI-first parallel kingdoms: agents co-create *on* human custody and use Pen IR; they do not bypass custody or form separate memory silos.
